e":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T16:39:44-08:00","id":1172422,"title":"","content":"This is specifically about Forsaken werewolves, or werewolves in general? In the former case, a Wolf-Blooded Tell shared before the First Change, esp. one that leaves a mark upon the transformed wolf-body after the Change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T16:45:24-08:00","id":1172424,"title":"","content":"I was going to suggest Fetishes. Maybe &quot;moonstones&quot;? Are you going for full Uratha, or are you just aiming for the general &quot;werewolf&quot; feel? Because many of the themes might work with Wolf-blooded, and you can have the Wolf-skin that lets them transform stand in for a wand.<br /> <br /> What is the exact theme you are aiming for with &quot;wand equivalent&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T16:46:49-08:00","id":1172425,"title":"","content":"<div cla